A||||6||DavidHenshaw||For Oreif||||1||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||02-21-2001||11:12 AM||||On the manifold exhaust leak thread you mentioned headers that are available. I've got leaks on my 2.8 and wonder if you could expand on the headers. Who has them, why are they better than sprints etc. Thanks.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||02-21-2001||12:46 PM||||Chris West at West Coast Fiero and FOCOA have headers. Headers are tuned for better flow. From what I have seen, The headers aren't all that beneficial on a stock 2.8L for their cost. The headers run about $650. The sprints run about $550. But if you ever upgrade to a 3.1 or 3.4 or nitros/turbo/SC the 2.8 they work great. If you plan on keeping your car stock, I think the sprints are the way to go, if you want to spend the money, since the rest of the exhaust stays stock. But the cost is high. I bought my sprints when the Fiero store first sold them and they were $100 less back then.<BR>(You can still get the 10% club discount on them too)<BR>I think it was 1FST2M6 who ran a set of headers across the dyno on a stock 2.8 and the gains were small. Like 4HP if I remember.<BR>The sprints offer the same gains as porting your stock manifolds but they look better, don't require special exhaust pipes, and don't crack. Mine have been on for 5 years and still look new.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DavidHenshaw||02-21-2001||07:41 PM||||Thanks Oreif, appreciate the info.<P>Dave <P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||02-21-2001||08:19 PM||||actually depending on your choice of headers you can get away with a full set that includes the "y" tube for $395.00. Far better price than the Sprints ( $600+ ) which don't even include a "y" tube.<P>Eric Nelson - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||02-21-2001||08:43 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>actually depending on your choice of headers you can get away with a full set that includes the "y" tube for $395.00. Far better price than the Sprints ( $600+ ) which don't even include a "y" tube.<P>Eric Nelson - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Sprints are $549, With Club Discount it's $494. You don't need a "Y" pipe because it uses the stock "Y" pipe as well as the rest of the system. (Just thought I'd clear that up) Do you have pic's of the $395 system? Any dyno or flow data? I'd be interested.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-21-2001).]||||reg||1
